  <Fragment slot="notes">
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>These are the standard textbook formulas, with returns added once a year. Yearly savings are added at the end of each year. Real returns go up and down, so treat the rate as an average guess and try a few.</p>
    <p>In the salary table, taxes are not included: use take-home pay if you want a closer answer.</p>
  </Fragment>
